The wasting fever is a sickness found in [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]]. It works on the soul: a healthy soul is a bundle of cloth, and a fevered one rots like a sack left in the rain, its threads coming apart until more than half is gone. Those it takes are thin to the point of starving, in pain, burned by sunlight and shy of it, and only half awake.

[[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]] holds it for a mild form of [[Phenomena/Althane/Sanguis Noxa|vampirism]], and its sufferers for lesser nightkin. The [[Org/Althane/Golden Sparrows|Sparrows]] found the early cases gathering around one freshwater well and sealed it, but new ones keep appearing across the city, and the [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]] is said not to want a cure.
